  "id": "COMPOUND:22637 - PROTEIN:6324",
  "verbalization": "Deglucocheirotoxol is consistently identified as a target of M-phase phosphoprotein 8 across three distinct paths, with a final score of 0.4924 in two of the paths and 0.4807 in the third. The shared target of MIP, Styraxlignolide B, and the compound [(1R,2R,3R,5S,6R,9R,10R,11R,13S,14S,19S)-19-acetyloxy-2,5,10,11-tetrahydroxy-6,9,13-trimethyl-12-oxo-7,17-dioxapentacyclo[11.6.0.03,9.06,10.016,19]nonadecan-14-yl] acetate suggests a common mechanism of action involving the regulation of the M-phase of the cell cycle. These compounds are all implicated in the targeting of M-phase phosphoprotein 8, which is a key player in the control of cell division and may be involved in the regulation of mitotic checkpoints. The evidence supports a potential role for Deglucocheirotoxol in modulating the activity of M-phase phosphoprotein 8, possibly through direct interaction or by influencing the cellular environment that affects its function. The consistent targeting of M-phase phosphoprotein 8 across different compounds implies a plausible mechanism of action, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact nature of the interaction.",
